cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "AI-to-learner knowledge transfer: a preregistered computational study on ECG age"
type: software
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
license: MIT
authors:
  - given-names: "KEYUR SHAILESHKUMAR"
    family-names: "PATEL"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-5261-043X"
    affiliation: "MSc Artificial Intelligence student, Department of Computer Science, Brunel University London, UK; Independent researcher"
abstract: >-
  Tests whether learners can acquire a perceptual skill they never had (telling younger from
  older adults from an ECG) using cues extracted from an AI. No human participants are involved: open-source
  language models and small neural networks are the learners. Conducted independently; not an
  official Brunel University London project.
keywords:
  - interpretability
  - knowledge transfer
  - machine teaching
  - ECG
  - preregistration
  - open science
